{"name":"Geranium Bud","hex":"#cfa1c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"geranium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any flowering plant of the genus Geranium, of family Geraniaceae.","Any flowering plant of the genus Pelargonium, of family Geraniaceae."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright red color tinted with orange, like that of a scarlet geranium (Pelargonium inquinans)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geranium"},{"term":"bud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ntcham."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A newly sprouted leaf or blossom that has not yet unfolded.","Something that has begun to develop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geranium","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium is a genus of 422 species of annual, biennial, and perennial plants that are commonly known as geraniums, hardy geraniums, or cranesbills. They are found throughout the temperate regions of the world and the mountains of the tropics, with the greatest diversity in the eastern part of the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg/330px-Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium","wikidata":"Q157211"},{"title":"Bud","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a bud is an undeveloped or embryonic shoot and normally occurs in the axil of a leaf or at the tip of a stem. Once formed, a bud may remain for some time in a dormant condition, or it may form a shoot immediately. Buds may be specialized to develop flowers or short shoots or may have the potential for general shoot development. The term bud is also used in zoology, where it refers to an outgrowth from the body which can develop into a new individual."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Fagus_sylvatica_bud.jpg/330px-Fagus_sylvatica_bud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bud","wikidata":"Q189838"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"bill\" and seed dispersal mechanism of G. pratense","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_sanguineum02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/500px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/1280px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/500px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close up of a wet geranium cultivar (probably 'Johnson's Blue') ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_(probably_'Johnson's_Blue').jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg/120px-Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg/250px-Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x",